<ProseLayout
  title="About Stockora Academy"
  lead="A free, independent learning site about stocks, trading and stock markets around the world."
  lastUpdated="2026-10-11"
>
  <h2>What Stockora is</h2>
  <p>
    Stockora Academy explains how the stock market works, from what a single share is, to how companies go public, to how
    markets in different countries differ. It is written in plain English for complete beginners (16+) and goes all the
    way to advanced topics. Every lesson aims to define its terms, show a worked example, and point to official sources.
  </p>
  <p>Austria is our "home" example, so you will find Austrian notes throughout, next to examples from other countries.</p>

  <h2>What "Academy" means here</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>"Academy" simply means "a place to learn".</strong> Stockora Academy is <strong>not</strong> an accredited
    school, university or training institution, and it does <strong>not</strong> award recognised qualifications. It is
    also <strong>not</strong> a bank, broker, investment adviser or any other regulated financial service.
  </p>

  <h2>Our rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Education only.</strong> No investment, tax or legal advice. No buy or sell recommendations.</li>
    <li><strong>No products pushed.</strong> No recommended stocks, funds, brokers, apps or crypto. No affiliate links. No ads.</li>
    <li><strong>No tracking.</strong> No analytics, no cookies, no third-party trackers. See the <a href={url('/privacy')}>Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sources and dates.</strong> Factual pages list their sources and when they were last reviewed. See
      <a href={url('/sources')}>Sources &amp; Methodology</a>.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Honest about risk.</strong> Investing can lose money. We say so clearly and often.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Please also read the <a href={url('/disclaimer')}>full disclaimer</a>.</p>
</ProseLayout>
